{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan-review remediation and collision resolution: the deterministic blockers were the nonstandard acceptance heading and missing Testing section; both are fixed with atomized observable criteria and real commands. Repository inspection also proved that id 15 is now occupied by the landed `sample, not the population` move from closed ticket amoral-natatorial-dog. The approved out-of-loop-proof content is therefore allocated the next free id, 16, while preserving move 15. Added the registry consumers required by current main: the mirrored gate-doc table, the plan-writing guide index, exact/scoped/rendering tests, and guide tests. A depends_on link to the closed predecessor was attempted for provenance but correctly rejected because rebar does not add blocking links to closed targets; the predecessor is cited directly in this plan and comment instead."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786565188334932001,"uuid":"9613bb44-5ec3-4fac-a0f7-69bca2f3cebd"}